# direction: specs/eravos.contrast-space.spec ADDENDUM 2026-11-27 (2) — one tool of the Contrast setup; research docs/research/rumble-techniques.md
identity:
  id: eravos.ripple ; label: Ripple ; domain: music ; family: bass ; icon: ≈ ; accent: "#ff5a3c"
  lineage: detuned low layers that beat (UK dubstep and grime low end, technique only), sub / mid split, tube drive
  novelty: detune in HERTZ (the swell rate is the same on every note), the sub kept clean beside a driven grind, the swell itself as a mod out
assembles (components, tools/music/components/<id>/ — never re-implemented here):
  unison-stack · saturator-tube
signal_dag:
  in → unison-stack
  unison-stack → saturator-tube
  saturator-tube → out
engine (per note, 6 at once, the oldest gives way):
  grind: voices 2…7 oscillators (wave) at the note + Grind octave, spread by unison-stack 1.1 (offsetHz: the outer two Beat Hz apart; cents
         from Detune; equal-power pans from Width) → low-pass (Cutoff, Reso, an envelope Env amt octaves above that falls over Env dec) → amp
         envelope → Grind level → saturator-tube (Drive dB, Bias) — one tube after all notes, so the voices' sums and differences are made there
  sub:   a sine on the note → the amp envelope → Sub level → out: never driven, never filtered, mono
  dive:  every oscillator starts Dive semitones above and falls to the note over Dive time (sub and grind together)
  out:   stereo audio → headroom → out · mod out ripple: |cos(π·Beat·t)| 0…1
mods in: beat (±6 Hz, spread across the voices as the layout's position) · cutoff (±4800 cents) · drive (±12 dB)
params: wave · voices · beat · detune · width · midOct · drive · bias · grind · sub · cutoff · res · fEnv · fDec · dive · diveTime · aA aD aS aR · octave · level
packs: factory — Floor Swell · Breathing Floor · Low Growl · Dive Bomb · Clean Pressure · Grime Square · Wide Rumble · Tremor Hit
acceptance:
  - the tool contract (TH.toolContract) · tests/p239-ripple.test.js: two voices at Beat 1.6 Hz swell 1.6 times a second (± 5 %) on two
    different notes; the sub band (< 1.5 × the note) is the same with Drive 0 and Drive 24 (the grind muted); a Dive 12 note starts an octave up
  - novelty (build/novelty-gate.mjs): every preset measured against all of ERAVOS; a TWIN or CLOSE is named (advisory) and answered here
  - null render: the components it changed (unison-stack 1.1, lfo 1.1) left Retro DCO 12/12, Swarm 14/14, Piano 11/11 unchanged (−60 dB)

